issue_context.body:
https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/blob/main/x-pack/plugin/transform/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/transform/checkpoint/DefaultCheckpointProvider.java#L116

When `remoteClusterResolver.resolve(transformConfig.getSource().getIndex())` returns no results, the `ActionListener<Map<String, long[]>> listener` is never called, causing the Transform to be started but stuck in `indexing`.

Any subsequent call to the `stats` API will cause the API call to timeout and the transport task to hang indefinitely.

### Steps to Reproduce

- spin up cluster
- add `Sample Web Logs` sample data
- create a working transform:
```
PUT _transform/last-log-from-clientip
{
  "source": {
    "index": [
      "kibana_sample_data_logs"
    ]
  },
  "latest": {
    "unique_key": [ 
      "clientip"
    ],
    "sort": "timestamp" 
  },
  "frequency": "1m", 
  "dest": {
    "index": "last-log-from-clientip"
  },
  "sync": { 
    "time": {
      "field": "timestamp",
      "delay": "60s"
    }
  },
  "retention_policy": { 
    "time": {
      "field": "timestamp",
      "max_age": "30d"
    }
  },
  "settings": {
    "max_page_search_size": 500
  }
}
```
- create a failing transform:
```
PUT _transform/last-log-from-clientip-failed
{
  "source": {
    "index": [
      "*:blah"
    ]
  },
  "latest": {
    "unique_key": [ 
      "clientip"
    ],
    "sort": "timestamp" 
  },
  "frequency": "1m", 
  "dest": {
    "index": "last-log-from-clientip-failed"
  },
  "sync": { 
    "time": {
      "field": "timestamp",
      "delay": "60s"
    }
  },
  "retention_policy": { 
    "time": {
      "field": "timestamp",
      "max_age": "30d"
    }
  },
  "settings": {
    "max_page_search_size": 500
  }
}
```

